# Week 9: House Price Data Analysis and Feature Engineering

## 1. Project Description

This project focuses on analyzing house sales data using Python. It explores property features, creates new features from existing columns, calculates price per square foot, and identifies potential outliers using statistical methods.

The project uses the `kc_house_data.csv` dataset to understand housing characteristics and price-related patterns.

## 2. Objectives

- Explore and understand the house sales dataset.
- Identify missing values and duplicate records.
- Analyze important property features.
- Create new features such as sale year, property age, and renovation status.
- Calculate price per square foot for living area and lot area.
- Visualize price-per-square-foot distributions using box plots.
- Detect potential outliers using the Interquartile Range (IQR) method.

## 3. Dataset Description

**Dataset Name:** `kc_house_data.csv`

The dataset contains information about house sales and property characteristics.

Important columns used in this project include:

- `price` – House sale price
- `bedrooms` – Number of bedrooms
- `bathrooms` – Number of bathrooms
- `sqft_living` – Interior living area in square feet
- `sqft_lot` – Lot area in square feet
- `grade` – Property construction and design grade
- `date` – House sale date
- `yr_built` – Year the house was built
- `yr_renovated` – Year of renovation, if applicable

